I. Job ProfileJob TitleProduction AssociateDepartmentProduction areas

Direct SupervisorShift SupervisorDirect SubordinatesNone

II. Job Summary：
Responsible for post in production safety, TPM, 5s and complete assigned jobs.

III. Job Functions and Duties

NO.Representative Duties

1Responsible to the workshop manager, obeying his/her technician’s and shift supervisor’s arrangement and deployment;

2Responsible for assigned job tasks, reporting any problems to the technician or supervisors;

3Responsible for handling post abnormalities in production, promptly reporting the results;

4Responsible for cleaning, management and safety of post, tooling, tools and equipment;

5Understanding Post Environmental Factors, Hazards and Control Methods;

6Conscientiously implementing integrated management system related documents;

7Storing post wastes by categories;

8Familiar with post material safety data sheets and emergency response measures;

9Other duties as assigned

10Nothing in the Position Description restricts management's right to assign or re-assign duties and responsibilities to this job at any time

IⅤ. Qualification

Job RequirementsLanguageLanguage spoken commonly in the workplace is English. - Ability to read, understand and comprehend documents such as safety rules, operating and maintenance instructions. Ability to interpret a variety of instructions furnished in written, oral, diagram, or schedule form. Ability to speak effectively and interact with other team members, engineers, leadership and customers.

Experience1-2 years of previous manufacturing expereince prefered, but will train.

EducationHigh School Diploma or General Education Degree (GED)

Physical ConditionThe employee is regularly required to stand the duration for long periods of time.  Turning at the waist, reaching, bending, squatting, and lifting up to 55lbs. repeatedly.

Other Requirementsa. Near Acuity-Clarity of vision at 20 inches or less. Use the factor when special and minute accuracy is demanded.
b. Far Acuity - Clarity of vision at 20 feet or more. Use the factor when visual effeciency in terms of far acuity is required day & night/dark conditions.
Must Pass a Tier ll Physical.                                                Must Pass a Background Check.

Knowledge, Skills & Abilities utilized on the jobProfessional  Knowledge, Skills1.Familiar with technology, quality, equipment operating instructions and environmental operating instructions;

2. Familiar with product appearance quality requirements and test methods;

3. Familiar with product safety and regulation;

4. Familiar with production orders and tracking sheets;

5. Familiar with tin side detector/steel ruler and application of post other measuring instruments;

6. Familiar with loading and washing machine operation and maintenance;

7. Familiar with post safety precautions;

Training RequiredNew Hire Orientation

Enterprise Profile, Rules and Regulations, Product Quality, Technology, Safety, System and Other Awareness Training

Printing process production flow

Post safety operation

Post Related Material Safety Data Sheet

Post Related Operating Instructions

V. Work Environment:
While performing the duties of this job, the employee is exposed to extreme heat. The noise level in the work environment is usually moderate to loud. Safety requirements for this position are safety glasses and steel-toed work shoes and ear plugs.

VI. Key Performance Indicators:

Must be 18 years of age or older.

